description:
BUG (crucial, user-blocking): the shipped plugin's hooks/hooks.json fails Claude Code hook validation at load with `Error: Hook load failed: expected record, received undefined at path ["hooks"]`. The file has TWO format defects vs the canonical Claude Code plugin hook schema (authoritative source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins.md, 'Migrate hooks' section): (1) missing the top-level `"hooks": { ... }` wrapper key (hence the error at path [hooks]); (2) the `type`/`command` are flattened as siblings of `matcher` instead of being nested inside a `"hooks": [ ... ]` array. This shipped undetected because NO sensor validates hooks/hooks.json structure. The file is not bundled into dist (ships as-is), so no rebuild is needed. matcher `startup|resume|clear|compact` is valid for SessionStart and must be preserved. This is a patch release (0.14.0 -> 0.14.1).

Corrected file content (write verbatim):
{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      { "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
        "hooks": [ { "type": "command", "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/context-monitor/repin.mjs\"" } ] }
    ]
  }
}
